    "reset": "ResetProfileState sets all five flags to zero.",
    "numeric_update": "A completed scalar numeric form ORs its produced five-bit vector into the old flags; it never clears a previously set flag.",
    "software_write": "A permitted full CORE_STATE system-register write replaces the flag field and may therefore clear flags.",
    "simultaneous": "The five bits are independent and have no priority; every produced bit is accumulated in the same update.",
    "rejected_operation": "An illegal or rejected scalar form leaves every flag unchanged and performs no profile-producer call.",
    "numeric_exception_trap": "Numeric exception outcomes do not themselves raise a synchronous PTO trap; encoding and legality faults remain separate pre-effect failures.",
    "trap_context": "Trap entry snapshots the complete CORE_STATE; successful recovery restores the manager-visible ECSTATE value, including all five flags.",
    "profile_boundary": "Architecture-owned forms have exact conditions below. Each supported profile-owned operation/type rule must return an exact flag vector; a missing rule rejects before effects under ADR 0037."
